   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Loaded Diction",
   "quote": "nefarii sceleris",
   "trans": "of the wicked crime",
   "body": "The narrator’s own judgement breaks in: the plan is a <em>nefarium scelus</em>, an \"unspeakable crime\". The heavy moral vocabulary darkens the scene just as Psyche prepares the lamp and blade.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The loaded phrase <em>nefarii sceleris</em> (‘wicked crime’) colours the narrative with the narrator’s condemnation, heightening the horror of what Psyche is about to attempt.\"",
