   "label": "Military Metaphor",
   "quote": "Veneris proeliis velitatus",
   "trans": "having skirmished in the battles of love",
   "body": "Love-making is cast as warfare: <em>Veneris proelia</em> are the \"battles of Venus\", and <em>velitatus</em> is a technical term for the light skirmishing that opens a fight. Spent from his \"campaign\", Cupid sinks into deep sleep.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The military metaphor <em>Veneris proeliis velitatus</em> wittily figures love-making as a battle, the skirmishing verb <em>velitatus</em> explaining why Cupid now lies defenceless in a <em>altus sopor</em>.\"",
